      "source": [
        "# Planning with HTN and Evolutionary Search Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements two toys:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A stdlib HTN planner with operators, methods, preconditions, effects, and a `LLMFallback` that kicks in when no method matches a compound task. The \"LLM\" is a scripted decomposer so the planner runs offline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A stdlib evolutionary search over arithmetic programs: grow expressions whose output minimizes `|f(x) - target|` over a test set. Evaluator is deterministic."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The trace shows the HTN planner decomposing a compound task (with a mid-plan LLM fallback) and the evolutionary loop converging on a target expression."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Extend the HTN planner with backtracking: when an operator's postcondition fails at runtime, roll back and try the next method.\n2. Add a LLM-method cache to ChatHTN: when the LLM decomposes task `T` in state pattern `P`, store the result. Re-check the method library first on the next call.\n3. Swap the evolutionary search evaluator to a real test suite. Evolve a sort function that passes 20 test cases; report generations to convergence.\n4. Read AlphaEvolve's evaluator design notes. Design an evaluator for a domain you care about (SQL query optimization, test-suite minimization, deployment YAML).\n5. Combine: use HTN to decompose a compound task into subtasks, then use evolutionary search on each subtask's primitive operator. Where does it shine, where does it over-engineer?"
      ]
    }
  ],
